{"parentUuid":"a33ccadc-c93d-4b50-a967-0cacbb1ddb69","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad57b07152710b373","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqMfbGDq4EcqYv5Eyz3d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LS7YpC8Q6mVkK4YKK9Huew","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\jobs_routes.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1995,"cache_read_input_tokens":64419,"output_tokens":178,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":101},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1995},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":178,"cache_read_input_tokens":64419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1995,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LS7YpC8Q6mVkK4YKK9Huew":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\jobs_routes.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0ed4f151-4a45-49d6-90d9-4f6c70219f45","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfqMfax7xcHNGTwTkc64j","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5d8b931e-763a-488e-a997-cbea54c4b039","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:54:59.694Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"5d8b931e-763a-488e-a997-cbea54c4b039","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b6cba788-ea7d-4fd0-94b4-156483cb0164","agentId":"ad57b07152710b373","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LS7YpC8Q6mVkK4YKK9Huew","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Web-form face of the Job (case) workflow.\n2\t\n3\tSame posture as ``cuore.web.dossier_routes``: a second router on the same\n4\tapp reusing ``cuore.web.routes``'s own page/dossier helpers, so rendering\n5\tstays identical to every other ``/v/{vin}`` page. Every form here degrades\n6\twith no JavaScript -- a stepper of plain GET/POST/redirect forms, same\n7\tconvention as ``/v/{vin}/dealer`` and ``/v/{vin}/notes``.\n8\t\n9\tJob UX pass (docs/research/JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md), 2026-10-08: every\n10\tmutating route below now redirects to ``?step=<the step it lives on>#<row\n11\tanchor>`` with a ``msg``/``mk`` (message/kind) query pair a toast reads --\n12\tnever to a different tab, never to a different step (fix #5).\n13\t\n14\t``cuore.services.jobs_bridge`` now carries the real guided-diagnostics\n15\tengine: ``edit_hypothesis``/``delete_hypothesis``/``undelete_hypothesis``/\n16\t``add_evidence``/``remove_evidence``/``resolve_evidence``/\n17\t``add_test_evidence``/``check_similar``/``step_registry``, and\n18\t``set_hypothesis`` enforces the confirm gate (open -> supported ->\n19\tconfirmed, refuted from any state; confirm needs >=1 passed/failed test\n20\tresult and 0 unresolved evidence_against -- fix #1) by raising\n21\t``jobs_bridge.RuleViolation`` *unconverted* -- this module's only job is to\n22\tcatch that (never let it 500) and redirect back to the same card with its\n23\t``reason``/``next_test`` shown inline, per the 409 {detail, next_test}\n24\tcontract. Every route below goes through ``jobs_bridge`` only -- no direct\n25\t``mes.jobs`` import here.\n26\t\"\"\"\n27\t\n28\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n29\t\n30\timport json\n31\tfrom typing import Any\n32\tfrom urllib.parse import quote\n33\t\n34\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Form, Request\n35\tfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\n36\t\n37\tfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n38\tfrom ..api.deps import require_token\n39\tfrom ..services import cases_bridge, dossier_bridge, jobs_bridge, tools_kb_bridge\n40\tfrom ..services.errors import BridgeError\n41\tfrom . import routes as web_routes\n42\t\n43\trouter = APIRouter(include_in_schema=False, dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n44\t\n45\ttry:  # fix #12: System picker is a taxonomy select, not free text\n46\t    from mes import systems as _mes_systems\n47\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the manual hypothesis form must still render\n48\t    _mes_systems = None\n49\t\n50\t\n51\tdef _systems_taxonomy() -> list[str]:\n52\t    if _mes_systems is None:\n53\t        return []\n54\t    try:\n55\t        return sorted({v.get(\"label\", k) for k, v in _mes_systems.systems().items()})\n56\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n57\t        return []\n58\t\n59\t\n60\tSYSTEMS_TAXONOMY: list[str] = _systems_taxonomy()\n61\t\n62\t\n63\tdef _rule_violation_msg(exc: \"jobs_bridge.RuleViolation\") -> str:\n64\t    \"\"\"One line out of a caught ``jobs_bridge.RuleViolation`` -- its own\n65\t    ``reason`` plus ``next_test`` when there is one, exactly what the toast\n66\t    shows (fix #1's 409 {detail, next_test} contract, rendered inline\n67\t    instead of as a raw HTTP body since this route serves an HTML form).\"\"\"\n68\t    reason = getattr(exc, \"reason\", None) or str(exc) or \"That wasn't allowed.\"\n69\t    next_test = getattr(exc, \"next_test\", \"\") or \"\"\n70\t    return f\"{reason} Next: {next_test}\" if next_test else reason\n71\t\n72\t\n73\tdef _step_redirect(vin: str, step: str = \"\", anchor: str = \"\", msg: str = \"\",\n74\t                   mk: str = \"ok\", extra: str = \"\") -> RedirectResponse:\n75\t    \"\"\"Every mutating route's one exit: back to the *same* step, never a\n76\t    different tab or step (fix #5) -- optionally with a one-line toast\n77\t    message/kind and any extra query the receiving page wants (e.g.\n78\t    ``confirm=<hyp_id>`` for the confirm-summary panel).\"\"\"\n79\t    parts = []\n80\t    if step:\n81\t        parts.append(f\"step={quote(str(step))}\")\n82\t    if msg:\n83\t        parts.append(f\"msg={quote(msg)}\")\n84\t        parts.append(f\"mk={quote(mk)}\")\n85\t    if extra:\n86\t        parts.append(extra)\n87\t    qs = (\"?\" + \"&\".join(parts)) if parts else \"\"\n88\t    frag = f\"#{anchor}\" if anchor else \"\"\n89\t    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/v/{vin}/job{qs}{frag}\", status_code=303)\n90\t\n91\t\n92\t@router.post(\"/tools-kb/inventory-form\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n93\tasync def tools_inventory_form(status: str = Form(...), tool: str = Form(...),\n94\t                               return_to: str = Form(default=\"/\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n95\t    \"\"\"The \"I have this / I don't\" button pair on the tools panel -- a\n96\t    garage-wide owned/not-owned list (``cuore.services.tools_kb_bridge``),\n97\t    not tied to any one vehicle, so it lives here rather than under\n98\t    ``/v/{vin}/...`` even though the tools panel itself renders on\n99\t    vehicle-scoped pages (job.html, maintenance.html).\"\"\"\n100\t    tools_kb_bridge.inventory_set(tool, status)\n101\t    return RedirectResponse(url=return_to or \"/\", status_code=303)\n102\t\n103\t\n104\tdef _job_page(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str = \"\", tools_step: str = \"\",\n105\t             step: str = \"\", **extra: Any) -> HTMLResponse:\n106\t    dossier = web_routes._dossier(vin)\n107\t    bar = web_routes._vehicle_bar(vin, dossier)\n108\t    job_view = jobs_bridge.build_job_view(vin, job_id or None, tools_step=tools_step or None)\n109\t    live_status = web_routes._status_strip()\n110\t    try:\n111\t        dossier_view = dossier_bridge.build_view(vin, dossier, live_status)\n112\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the job page must still render\n113\t        dossier_view = {\"verdict\": None, \"open_work\": [], \"codes\": [],\n114\t                        \"code_counts\": {}, \"attempted\": []}\n115\t    active_codes = [c[\"code\"] for c in dossier_view.get(\"codes\", [])\n116\t                    if c.get(\"status\") == \"ACTIVE\"]\n117\t    try:\n118\t        case_prefill = cases_bridge.prefill(vin, active_codes)\n119\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- case memory must never 500 the job page\n120\t        case_prefill = None\n121\t\n122\t    # --- display-only reshaping of job_view for this render (fix #11/#13):\n123\t    # active (non-deleted) hypotheses ranked by net evidence with the\n124\t    # leading one pinned first; deleted ones split out for an Undo row.\n125\t    # ``jobs_bridge.suggested_hypotheses`` already dedupes+ranks its own\n126\t    # list, so the suggestions themselves need no further work here --\n127\t    # job.html just slices the first 3 off for \"top\" vs. \"Show N more\".\n128\t    # Never mutates the stored job; this dict is built fresh per request.\n129\t    hyps = list((job_view.get(\"job\") or {}).get(\"hypotheses\") or [])\n130\t    active_hyps = [h for h in hyps if not h.get(\"deleted\")]\n131\t    deleted_hyps = [h for h in hyps if h.get(\"deleted\")]\n132\t    active_hyps.sort(\n133\t        key=lambda h: (len(h.get(\"evidence_for\") or []) - len(h.get(\"evidence_against\") or [])),\n134\t        reverse=True,\n135\t    )\n136\t    if job_view.get(\"job\"):\n137\t        job_view[\"job\"][\"hypotheses\"] = active_hyps\n138\t    job_view[\"deleted_hypotheses\"] = deleted_hyps\n139\t\n140\t    # Toast/flash state from a mutating route's redirect (fix #5) -- read\n141\t    # straight off the query string so this works with zero JavaScript;\n142\t    # job.js upgrades the same params into a nicer dismissable toast.\n143\t    qp = request.query_params\n144\t    flash_msg = qp.get(\"msg\") or \"\"\n145\t    flash_kind = qp.get(\"mk\") or \"ok\"\n146\t    confirm_pending = qp.get(\"confirm\") or \"\"\n147\t    undo_hyp = qp.get(\"undo_hyp\") or \"\"\n148\t\n149\t    # `view` carries the full dossier view -- the shape _verdict_card.html,\n150\t    # _codes_table.html and _open_work.html already expect everywhere else\n151\t    # they're included; `job_view` carries the Job-specific data only\n152\t    # job.html itself reads.\n153\t    response = web_routes._page(request, \"job.html\", vin=vin, bar=bar, view=dossier_view,\n154\t                                job_view=job_view, case_prefill=case_prefill,\n155\t                                active_codes=active_codes, tab=\"job\", step=step,\n156\t                                flash_msg=flash_msg, flash_kind=flash_kind,\n157\t                                confirm_pending=confirm_pending, undo_hyp=undo_hyp,\n158\t                                systems_taxonomy=SYSTEMS_TAXONOMY, **extra)\n159\t    web_routes._set_active_vehicle(response, vin)\n160\t    return response\n161\t\n162\t\n163\t@router.get(\"/v/{vin}/job\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n164\tdef job_page(request: Request, vin: str, tools_step: str = \"\", step: str = \"\") -> HTMLResponse:\n165\t    \"\"\"The current (or most recent) job for this vehicle, one step per\n166\t    screen -- ``step`` is the only query param this page reads to pick\n167\t    which of the 12 steps is the full screen (default: the flow's own\n168\t    current step, resolved inside job.html itself).\"\"\"\n169\t    return _job_page(request, vin, tools_step=tools_step, step=step)\n170\t\n171\t\n172\t@router.get(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n173\tdef job_page_one(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, tools_step: str = \"\",\n174\t                 step: str = \"\") -> HTMLResponse:\n175\t    \"\"\"One specific job by id -- e.g. a closed case from this car's history.\"\"\"\n176\t    return _job_page(request, vin, job_id=job_id, tools_step=tools_step, step=step)\n177\t\n178\t\n179\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/open\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n180\tasync def job_open(request: Request, vin: str,\n181\t                   technician: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n182\t                   complaint: str = Form(default=\"\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n183\t    \"\"\"Step 1: open a new case for this vehicle, in the driver's own words.\"\"\"\n184\t    jobs_bridge.open_job(vin, technician=technician, complaint=complaint)\n185\t    return _step_redirect(vin, \"1\", msg=\"Case opened.\", mk=\"ok\")\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n189\tasync def hypothesis_add(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str,\n190\t                         text: str = Form(...), system: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n191\t                         next_test: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n192\t                         likelihood: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n193\t                         codes: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n194\t                         by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n195\t                         step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n196\t    \"\"\"Step 7: add a hypothesis by hand (fix #12: System is a taxonomy pick,\n197\t    Linked codes a multi-select of open DTCs, Likelihood Low/Med/High).\"\"\"\n198\t    code_list = [c.strip() for c in codes.split(\",\") if c.strip()]\n199\t    likelihood_val = likelihood.strip().lower() or None\n200\t    try:\n201\t        hyp = jobs_bridge.add_hypothesis(job_id, text, system=system, next_test=next_test,\n202\t                                         codes=code_list or None, likelihood=likelihood_val,\n203\t                                         by=by.strip() or None)\n204\t    except BridgeError as exc:\n205\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=\"add-hypothesis\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n206\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp['id']}\", msg=\"Hypothesis added.\", mk=\"ok\")\n207\t\n208\t\n209\t@router.get(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/similar\")\n210\tdef hypothesis_similar(vin: str, job_id: str, text: str = \"\", system: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n211\t    \"\"\"Fix #11's \"Similar to ... -- merge?\" prompt, read live as the tech\n212\t    types (job.js debounces this) -- thin pass-through to\n213\t    ``jobs_bridge.check_similar``, the real token-overlap check against the\n214\t    job on file, so the prompt is never a client-side guess. No JS -> no\n215\t    prompt, no behaviour change: the manual-add form still saves a new\n216\t    hypothesis either way.\"\"\"\n217\t    try:\n218\t        match = jobs_bridge.check_similar(job_id, text, system)\n219\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a hint must never 500\n220\t        match = None\n221\t    if not match:\n222\t        return {\"similar\": None}\n223\t    return {\"similar\": {\"id\": match[\"id\"], \"text\": match[\"text\"]}}\n224\t\n225\t\n226\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/suggested\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n227\tasync def hypothesis_add_suggested(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str,\n228\t                                   text: str = Form(...), system: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n229\t                                   next_test: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n230\t                                   evidence_for: str = Form(default=\"[]\"),\n231\t                                   evidence_against: str = Form(default=\"[]\"),\n232\t                                   step: str = Form(default=\"7\")\n233\t                                   ) -> RedirectResponse:\n234\t    \"\"\"Step 7: promote one of the auto-suggested hypotheses, with its real\n235\t    evidence attached in the same step -- the refs travel as a hidden JSON\n236\t    field rather than being retyped, so nothing here can invent evidence\n237\t    that was not already shown on the page.\"\"\"\n238\t    suggestion = {\n239\t        \"text\": text, \"system\": system, \"next_test\": next_test,\n240\t        \"evidence_for\": json.loads(evidence_for) if evidence_for.strip() else [],\n241\t        \"evidence_against\": json.loads(evidence_against) if evidence_against.strip() else [],\n242\t    }\n243\t    hyp = jobs_bridge.add_suggested_hypothesis(job_id, suggestion)\n244\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp['id']}\",\n245\t                          msg=\"Hypothesis added from suggestion.\", mk=\"ok\")\n246\t\n247\t\n248\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/status\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n249\tasync def hypothesis_set_status(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n250\t                                status: str = Form(...), step: str = Form(default=\"7\"),\n251\t                                ack: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n252\t                                by: str = Form(default=\"\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n253\t    \"\"\"Step 7: the status buttons -- open / supported / refuted / confirmed.\n254\t\n255\t    Fix #1: ``jobs_bridge.set_hypothesis`` itself enforces the path (open ->\n256\t    supported -> confirmed, refuted from any state) and the confirm gate\n257\t    (>=1 passed/failed test evidence_for, 0 unresolved evidence_against),\n258\t    raising ``jobs_bridge.RuleViolation`` -- caught below and shown inline\n259\t    (the 409 {detail, next_test} contract, rendered as this HTML form's own\n260\t    toast), never a 500 and never silently accepted. ``confirmed``\n261\t    additionally needs a second tap (``ack=1``): the first tap just\n262\t    redirects back with ``confirm=<hyp_id>`` so job.html renders the\n263\t    evidence-summary panel job.js promotes into a modal -- its own \"confirm\n264\t    again\" button is what actually sends ``ack=1``; if the gate would have\n265\t    refused anyway, that second POST catches the same RuleViolation. ``by``\n266\t    (who) rides along so the engine can stamp confirmed_by/at.\"\"\"\n267\t    if status == \"confirmed\" and ack != \"1\":\n268\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", extra=f\"confirm={hyp_id}\")\n269\t\n270\t    try:\n271\t        jobs_bridge.set_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, status=status, by=by.strip() or None)\n272\t    except jobs_bridge.RuleViolation as exc:\n273\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\",\n274\t                              msg=_rule_violation_msg(exc), mk=\"err\")\n275\t    except BridgeError as exc:\n276\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n277\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=f\"Status set to {status}.\",\n278\t                          mk=\"ok\")\n279\t\n280\t\n281\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/next_test\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n282\tasync def hypothesis_set_next_test(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n283\t                                   next_test: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n284\t                                   step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n285\t    jobs_bridge.set_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, next_test=next_test)\n286\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Saved.\", mk=\"ok\")\n287\t\n288\t\n289\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/edit\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n290\tasync def hypothesis_edit(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n291\t                          text: str = Form(default=\"\"), system: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n292\t                          next_test: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n293\t                          likelihood: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n294\t                          codes: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n295\t                          by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n296\t                          step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n297\t    \"\"\"Fix #2: Edit -- any hypothesis field except status/evidence, which go\n298\t    through their own gated routes so editing can never route around the\n299\t    confirm gate.\"\"\"\n300\t    kw: dict[str, Any] = {}\n301\t    if text.strip():\n302\t        kw[\"text\"] = text\n303\t    if system:\n304\t        kw[\"system\"] = system\n305\t    if next_test:\n306\t        kw[\"next_test\"] = next_test\n307\t    if likelihood:\n308\t        kw[\"likelihood\"] = likelihood.strip().lower()\n309\t    if codes.strip():\n310\t        kw[\"codes\"] = [c.strip() for c in codes.split(\",\") if c.strip()]\n311\t    if not kw:\n312\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Nothing to save.\", mk=\"warn\")\n313\t    try:\n314\t        jobs_bridge.edit_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, by=by.strip() or None, **kw)\n315\t    except BridgeError as exc:\n316\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n317\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Hypothesis updated.\", mk=\"ok\")\n318\t\n319\t\n320\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/evidence\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n321\tasync def hypothesis_evidence(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n322\t                              side: str = Form(default=\"for\"),\n323\t                              kind: str = Form(default=\"observation\"),\n324\t                              ref_id: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n325\t                              label: str = Form(...),\n326\t                              op: str = Form(default=\"add\"),\n327\t                              by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n328\t                              step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n329\t    \"\"\"Fix #2: + Evidence for / + Evidence against, and the remove side of\n330\t    the same picker -- thin pass-through to ``jobs_bridge.add_evidence``/\n331\t    ``remove_evidence``, which is what the confirm gate itself reads, so an\n332\t    item linked here is real evidence for fix #1 the moment it's added.\"\"\"\n333\t    side = side if side in (\"for\", \"against\") else \"for\"\n334\t    if op == \"remove\":\n335\t        try:\n336\t            jobs_bridge.remove_evidence(job_id, hyp_id, side, ref_id or label,\n337\t                                        ref_kind=kind or None, by=by.strip() or None)\n338\t        except BridgeError as exc:\n339\t            return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n340\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Evidence removed.\",\n341\t                              mk=\"ok\", extra=f\"undo_ev={hyp_id}:{side}:{quote(label)}\")\n342\t\n343\t    ref = {\"kind\": kind or \"observation\", \"id\": ref_id or label, \"label\": label}\n344\t    try:\n345\t        jobs_bridge.add_evidence(job_id, hyp_id, side, ref, by=by.strip() or None)\n346\t    except BridgeError as exc:\n347\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n348\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\",\n349\t                          msg=f\"Evidence {'for' if side == 'for' else 'against'} added.\", mk=\"ok\")\n350\t\n351\t\n352\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/delete\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n353\tasync def hypothesis_delete(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n354\t                            by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n355\t                            step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n356\t    \"\"\"Fix #2: Delete, soft (``jobs_bridge.delete_hypothesis``) -- the card\n357\t    itself stays on the audit trail; the undo offered in the toast is\n358\t    :func:`hypothesis_undelete` below.\"\"\"\n359\t    try:\n360\t        jobs_bridge.delete_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, by=by.strip() or None)\n361\t    except BridgeError as exc:\n362\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=\"hypotheses\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n363\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=\"hypotheses\", msg=\"Hypothesis deleted.\", mk=\"ok\",\n364\t                          extra=f\"undo_hyp={hyp_id}\")\n365\t\n366\t\n367\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/undelete\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n368\tasync def hypothesis_undelete(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n369\t                              by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n370\t                              step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n371\t    try:\n372\t        jobs_bridge.undelete_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, by=by.strip() or None)\n373\t    except BridgeError as exc:\n374\t        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n375\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Hypothesis restored.\", mk=\"ok\")\n376\t\n377\t\n378\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/actions\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n379\tasync def action_add(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str,\n380\t                     kind: str = Form(...), text: str = Form(...),\n381\t                     step: str = Form(default=\"9\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n382\t    \"\"\"Step 9: record one repair action -- test, inspection, repair, part,\n383\t    clear, or a free-text note.\"\"\"\n384\t    jobs_bridge.add_action(job_id, kind, text)\n385\t    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=\"actions\", msg=\"Action recorded.\", mk=\"ok\")\n386\t\n387\t\n388\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/tools-review\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n389\tasync def tools_review_add(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n390\t    \"\"\"Step 12: the mandatory \"tools used\" review -- what was actually used\n391\t    at release, right/wrong/unsure with a reason, anything missing, and\n392\t    what he'd buy next time. Field names are dynamic (one triplet per\n393\t    recommended tool, keyed by tool key) because the recommended-tool list\n394\t    itself is dynamic, so this reads the raw form rather than a fixed\n395\t    Pydantic/Form model -- same reasoning job_page's tools panel is built\n396\t    for a variable-length list.\n397\t    \"\"\"\n398\t    form = await request.form()\n399\t\n400\t    def _get(key: str) -> str:\n401\t        v = form.get(key)\n402\t        return str(v).strip() if v is not None else \"\"\n403\t\n404\t    step = _get(\"step\") or \"diagnostics\"\n405\t    tools_used: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n406\t    for key in form.keys():\n407\t        if key.startswith(\"used__\") and _get(key):\n408\t            tool_key = key[len(\"used__\"):]\n409\t            tools_used.append({\n410\t                \"tool\": tool_key,\n411\t                \"was_right\": _get(f\"right__{tool_key}\") or \"unsure\",\n412\t                \"note\": _get(f\"note__{tool_key}\"),\n413\t            })\n414\t    for i in range(1, 4):\n415\t        name = _get(f\"extra{i}_name\")\n416\t        if name:\n417\t            tools_used.append({\n418\t                \"tool\": name,\n419\t                \"was_right\": _get(f\"extra{i}_right\") or \"unsure\",\n420\t                \"note\": _get(f\"extra{i}_note\"),\n421\t            })\n422\t\n423\t    missing_tools = [m.strip() for m in _get(\"missing_tools\").split(\",\") if m.strip()]\n424\t\n425\t    would_buy: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n426\t    for i in range(1, 4):\n427\t        name = _get(f\"buy{i}_name\")\n428\t        if name:\n429\t            would_buy.append({\"name\": name, \"why\": _get(f\"buy{i}_why\")})\n430\t\n431\t    time_min_raw = _get(\"time_min\")\n432\t    time_min = float(time_min_raw) if time_min_raw else None\n433\t\n434\t    jobs_bridge.add_tool_usage(vin, step, job_id, by=_get(\"by\"), tools_used=tools_used,\n435\t                               missing_tools=missing_tools, would_buy=would_buy,\n436\t                               time_min=time_min)\n437\t    return _step_redirect(vin, \"12\", anchor=\"outcome\", msg=\"Tools review saved.\", mk=\"ok\")\n438\t\n439\t\n440\t@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/close\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n441\tasync def job_close(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str,\n442\t                    outcome: str = Form(...),\n443\t                    codes_returned: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n444\t                    verdict: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n445\t                    tools_review_skip_reason: str = Form(default=\"\")) -> HTMLResponse:\n446\t    \"\"\"Step 12: close the case. Outcome is required -- a job can never be\n447\t    closed with no stated result. Also gated on the tools-used review\n448\t    (see ``jobs_bridge.close_job``) -- ``tools_review_skip_reason`` lets a\n449\t    mechanic close without filling the review, but only by stating why.\"\"\"\n450\t    codes = [c.strip() for c in codes_returned.split(\",\") if c.strip()]\n451\t    error = None\n452\t    try:\n453\t        jobs_bridge.close_job(job_id, outcome, codes_returned=codes or None,\n454\t                              verdict=verdict or None,\n455\t                              tools_review_skip_reason=tools_review_skip_reason)\n456\t    except BridgeError as exc:\n457\t        error = str(exc)\n458\t    # Rendered directly (no redirect) -- the close form lives on step 12's\n459\t    # screen, so that's the screen the re-render must show, regardless of\n460\t    # the flow's own current-step opinion, or a refusal would render onto\n461\t    # whatever step happens to be current and never be seen.\n462\t    return _job_page(request, vin, job_id=job_id, close_error=error, step=\"12\")\n463\t\n464\t\n465\t__all__ = [\"router\"]\n466\t"}]},"uuid":"d0b4838c-932a-4383-b0b8-cb25b03a5624","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:54:59.728Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\jobs_routes.py","content":"\"\"\"Web-form face of the Job (case) workflow.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore.web.dossier_routes``: a second router on the same\napp reusing ``cuore.web.routes``'s own page/dossier helpers, so rendering\nstays identical to every other ``/v/{vin}`` page. Every form here degrades\nwith no JavaScript -- a stepper of plain GET/POST/redirect forms, same\nconvention as ``/v/{vin}/dealer`` and ``/v/{vin}/notes``.\n\nJob UX pass (docs/research/JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md), 2026-10-08: every\nmutating route below now redirects to ``?step=<the step it lives on>#<row\nanchor>`` with a ``msg``/``mk`` (message/kind) query pair a toast reads --\nnever to a different tab, never to a different step (fix #5).\n\n``cuore.services.jobs_bridge`` now carries the real guided-diagnostics\nengine: ``edit_hypothesis``/``delete_hypothesis``/``undelete_hypothesis``/\n``add_evidence``/``remove_evidence``/``resolve_evidence``/\n``add_test_evidence``/``check_similar``/``step_registry``, and\n``set_hypothesis`` enforces the confirm gate (open -> supported ->\nconfirmed, refuted from any state; confirm needs >=1 passed/failed test\nresult and 0 unresolved evidence_against -- fix #1) by raising\n``jobs_bridge.RuleViolation`` *unconverted* -- this module's only job is to\ncatch that (never let it 500) and redirect back to the same card with its\n``reason``/``next_test`` shown inline, per the 409 {detail, next_test}\ncontract. Every route below goes through ``jobs_bridge`` only -- no direct\n``mes.jobs`` import here.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Form, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom ..api.deps import require_token\nfrom ..services import cases_bridge, dossier_bridge, jobs_bridge, tools_kb_bridge\nfrom ..services.errors import BridgeError\nfrom . import routes as web_routes\n\nrouter = APIRouter(include_in_schema=False, dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n\ntry:  # fix #12: System picker is a taxonomy select, not free text\n    from mes import systems as _mes_systems\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the manual hypothesis form must still render\n    _mes_systems = None\n\n\ndef _systems_taxonomy() -> list[str]:\n    if _mes_systems is None:\n        return []\n    try:\n        return sorted({v.get(\"label\", k) for k, v in _mes_systems.systems().items()})\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return []\n\n\nSYSTEMS_TAXONOMY: list[str] = _systems_taxonomy()\n\n\ndef _rule_violation_msg(exc: \"jobs_bridge.RuleViolation\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"One line out of a caught ``jobs_bridge.RuleViolation`` -- its own\n    ``reason`` plus ``next_test`` when there is one, exactly what the toast\n    shows (fix #1's 409 {detail, next_test} contract, rendered inline\n    instead of as a raw HTTP body since this route serves an HTML form).\"\"\"\n    reason = getattr(exc, \"reason\", None) or str(exc) or \"That wasn't allowed.\"\n    next_test = getattr(exc, \"next_test\", \"\") or \"\"\n    return f\"{reason} Next: {next_test}\" if next_test else reason\n\n\ndef _step_redirect(vin: str, step: str = \"\", anchor: str = \"\", msg: str = \"\",\n                   mk: str = \"ok\", extra: str = \"\") -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Every mutating route's one exit: back to the *same* step, never a\n    different tab or step (fix #5) -- optionally with a one-line toast\n    message/kind and any extra query the receiving page wants (e.g.\n    ``confirm=<hyp_id>`` for the confirm-summary panel).\"\"\"\n    parts = []\n    if step:\n        parts.append(f\"step={quote(str(step))}\")\n    if msg:\n        parts.append(f\"msg={quote(msg)}\")\n        parts.append(f\"mk={quote(mk)}\")\n    if extra:\n        parts.append(extra)\n    qs = (\"?\" + \"&\".join(parts)) if parts else \"\"\n    frag = f\"#{anchor}\" if anchor else \"\"\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/v/{vin}/job{qs}{frag}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/tools-kb/inventory-form\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def tools_inventory_form(status: str = Form(...), tool: str = Form(...),\n                               return_to: str = Form(default=\"/\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"The \"I have this / I don't\" button pair on the tools panel -- a\n    garage-wide owned/not-owned list (``cuore.services.tools_kb_bridge``),\n    not tied to any one vehicle, so it lives here rather than under\n    ``/v/{vin}/...`` even though the tools panel itself renders on\n    vehicle-scoped pages (job.html, maintenance.html).\"\"\"\n    tools_kb_bridge.inventory_set(tool, status)\n    return RedirectResponse(url=return_to or \"/\", status_code=303)\n\n\ndef _job_page(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str = \"\", tools_step: str = \"\",\n             step: str = \"\", **extra: Any) -> HTMLResponse:\n    dossier = web_routes._dossier(vin)\n    bar = web_routes._vehicle_bar(vin, dossier)\n    job_view = jobs_bridge.build_job_view(vin, job_id or None, tools_step=tools_step or None)\n    live_status = web_routes._status_strip()\n    try:\n        dossier_view = dossier_bridge.build_view(vin, dossier, live_status)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the job page must still render\n        dossier_view = {\"verdict\": None, \"open_work\": [], \"codes\": [],\n                        \"code_counts\": {}, \"attempted\": []}\n    active_codes = [c[\"code\"] for c in dossier_view.get(\"codes\", [])\n                    if c.get(\"status\") == \"ACTIVE\"]\n    try:\n        case_prefill = cases_bridge.prefill(vin, active_codes)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- case memory must never 500 the job page\n        case_prefill = None\n\n    # --- display-only reshaping of job_view for this render (fix #11/#13):\n    # active (non-deleted) hypotheses ranked by net evidence with the\n    # leading one pinned first; deleted ones split out for an Undo row.\n    # ``jobs_bridge.suggested_hypotheses`` already dedupes+ranks its own\n    # list, so the suggestions themselves need no further work here --\n    # job.html just slices the first 3 off for \"top\" vs. \"Show N more\".\n    # Never mutates the stored job; this dict is built fresh per request.\n    hyps = list((job_view.get(\"job\") or {}).get(\"hypotheses\") or [])\n    active_hyps = [h for h in hyps if not h.get(\"deleted\")]\n    deleted_hyps = [h for h in hyps if h.get(\"deleted\")]\n    active_hyps.sort(\n        key=lambda h: (len(h.get(\"evidence_for\") or []) - len(h.get(\"evidence_against\") or [])),\n        reverse=True,\n    )\n    if job_view.get(\"job\"):\n        job_view[\"job\"][\"hypotheses\"] = active_hyps\n    job_view[\"deleted_hypotheses\"] = deleted_hyps\n\n    # Toast/flash state from a mutating route's redirect (fix #5) -- read\n    # straight off the query string so this works with zero JavaScript;\n    # job.js upgrades the same params into a nicer dismissable toast.\n    qp = request.query_params\n    flash_msg = qp.get(\"msg\") or \"\"\n    flash_kind = qp.get(\"mk\") or \"ok\"\n    confirm_pending = qp.get(\"confirm\") or \"\"\n    undo_hyp = qp.get(\"undo_hyp\") or \"\"\n\n    # `view` carries the full dossier view -- the shape _verdict_card.html,\n    # _codes_table.html and _open_work.html already expect everywhere else\n    # they're included; `job_view` carries the Job-specific data only\n    # job.html itself reads.\n    response = web_routes._page(request, \"job.html\", vin=vin, bar=bar, view=dossier_view,\n                                job_view=job_view, case_prefill=case_prefill,\n                                active_codes=active_codes, tab=\"job\", step=step,\n                                flash_msg=flash_msg, flash_kind=flash_kind,\n                                confirm_pending=confirm_pending, undo_hyp=undo_hyp,\n                                systems_taxonomy=SYSTEMS_TAXONOMY, **extra)\n    web_routes._set_active_vehicle(response, vin)\n    return response\n\n\n@router.get(\"/v/{vin}/job\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef job_page(request: Request, vin: str, tools_step: str = \"\", step: str = \"\") -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"The current (or most recent) job for this vehicle, one step per\n    screen -- ``step`` is the only query param this page reads to pick\n    which of the 12 steps is the full screen (default: the flow's own\n    current step, resolved inside job.html itself).\"\"\"\n    return _job_page(request, vin, tools_step=tools_step, step=step)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef job_page_one(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, tools_step: str = \"\",\n                 step: str = \"\") -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"One specific job by id -- e.g. a closed case from this car's history.\"\"\"\n    return _job_page(request, vin, job_id=job_id, tools_step=tools_step, step=step)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/open\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def job_open(request: Request, vin: str,\n                   technician: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                   complaint: str = Form(default=\"\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Step 1: open a new case for this vehicle, in the driver's own words.\"\"\"\n    jobs_bridge.open_job(vin, technician=technician, complaint=complaint)\n    return _step_redirect(vin, \"1\", msg=\"Case opened.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def hypothesis_add(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str,\n                         text: str = Form(...), system: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                         next_test: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                         likelihood: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                         codes: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                         by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                         step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Step 7: add a hypothesis by hand (fix #12: System is a taxonomy pick,\n    Linked codes a multi-select of open DTCs, Likelihood Low/Med/High).\"\"\"\n    code_list = [c.strip() for c in codes.split(\",\") if c.strip()]\n    likelihood_val = likelihood.strip().lower() or None\n    try:\n        hyp = jobs_bridge.add_hypothesis(job_id, text, system=system, next_test=next_test,\n                                         codes=code_list or None, likelihood=likelihood_val,\n                                         by=by.strip() or None)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=\"add-hypothesis\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp['id']}\", msg=\"Hypothesis added.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.get(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/similar\")\ndef hypothesis_similar(vin: str, job_id: str, text: str = \"\", system: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Fix #11's \"Similar to ... -- merge?\" prompt, read live as the tech\n    types (job.js debounces this) -- thin pass-through to\n    ``jobs_bridge.check_similar``, the real token-overlap check against the\n    job on file, so the prompt is never a client-side guess. No JS -> no\n    prompt, no behaviour change: the manual-add form still saves a new\n    hypothesis either way.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        match = jobs_bridge.check_similar(job_id, text, system)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a hint must never 500\n        match = None\n    if not match:\n        return {\"similar\": None}\n    return {\"similar\": {\"id\": match[\"id\"], \"text\": match[\"text\"]}}\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/suggested\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def hypothesis_add_suggested(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str,\n                                   text: str = Form(...), system: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                                   next_test: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                                   evidence_for: str = Form(default=\"[]\"),\n                                   evidence_against: str = Form(default=\"[]\"),\n                                   step: str = Form(default=\"7\")\n                                   ) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Step 7: promote one of the auto-suggested hypotheses, with its real\n    evidence attached in the same step -- the refs travel as a hidden JSON\n    field rather than being retyped, so nothing here can invent evidence\n    that was not already shown on the page.\"\"\"\n    suggestion = {\n        \"text\": text, \"system\": system, \"next_test\": next_test,\n        \"evidence_for\": json.loads(evidence_for) if evidence_for.strip() else [],\n        \"evidence_against\": json.loads(evidence_against) if evidence_against.strip() else [],\n    }\n    hyp = jobs_bridge.add_suggested_hypothesis(job_id, suggestion)\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp['id']}\",\n                          msg=\"Hypothesis added from suggestion.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/status\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def hypothesis_set_status(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n                                status: str = Form(...), step: str = Form(default=\"7\"),\n                                ack: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                                by: str = Form(default=\"\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Step 7: the status buttons -- open / supported / refuted / confirmed.\n\n    Fix #1: ``jobs_bridge.set_hypothesis`` itself enforces the path (open ->\n    supported -> confirmed, refuted from any state) and the confirm gate\n    (>=1 passed/failed test evidence_for, 0 unresolved evidence_against),\n    raising ``jobs_bridge.RuleViolation`` -- caught below and shown inline\n    (the 409 {detail, next_test} contract, rendered as this HTML form's own\n    toast), never a 500 and never silently accepted. ``confirmed``\n    additionally needs a second tap (``ack=1``): the first tap just\n    redirects back with ``confirm=<hyp_id>`` so job.html renders the\n    evidence-summary panel job.js promotes into a modal -- its own \"confirm\n    again\" button is what actually sends ``ack=1``; if the gate would have\n    refused anyway, that second POST catches the same RuleViolation. ``by``\n    (who) rides along so the engine can stamp confirmed_by/at.\"\"\"\n    if status == \"confirmed\" and ack != \"1\":\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", extra=f\"confirm={hyp_id}\")\n\n    try:\n        jobs_bridge.set_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, status=status, by=by.strip() or None)\n    except jobs_bridge.RuleViolation as exc:\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\",\n                              msg=_rule_violation_msg(exc), mk=\"err\")\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=f\"Status set to {status}.\",\n                          mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/next_test\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def hypothesis_set_next_test(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n                                   next_test: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                                   step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    jobs_bridge.set_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, next_test=next_test)\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Saved.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/edit\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def hypothesis_edit(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n                          text: str = Form(default=\"\"), system: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                          next_test: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                          likelihood: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                          codes: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                          by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                          step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Fix #2: Edit -- any hypothesis field except status/evidence, which go\n    through their own gated routes so editing can never route around the\n    confirm gate.\"\"\"\n    kw: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    if text.strip():\n        kw[\"text\"] = text\n    if system:\n        kw[\"system\"] = system\n    if next_test:\n        kw[\"next_test\"] = next_test\n    if likelihood:\n        kw[\"likelihood\"] = likelihood.strip().lower()\n    if codes.strip():\n        kw[\"codes\"] = [c.strip() for c in codes.split(\",\") if c.strip()]\n    if not kw:\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Nothing to save.\", mk=\"warn\")\n    try:\n        jobs_bridge.edit_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, by=by.strip() or None, **kw)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Hypothesis updated.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/evidence\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def hypothesis_evidence(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n                              side: str = Form(default=\"for\"),\n                              kind: str = Form(default=\"observation\"),\n                              ref_id: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                              label: str = Form(...),\n                              op: str = Form(default=\"add\"),\n                              by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                              step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Fix #2: + Evidence for / + Evidence against, and the remove side of\n    the same picker -- thin pass-through to ``jobs_bridge.add_evidence``/\n    ``remove_evidence``, which is what the confirm gate itself reads, so an\n    item linked here is real evidence for fix #1 the moment it's added.\"\"\"\n    side = side if side in (\"for\", \"against\") else \"for\"\n    if op == \"remove\":\n        try:\n            jobs_bridge.remove_evidence(job_id, hyp_id, side, ref_id or label,\n                                        ref_kind=kind or None, by=by.strip() or None)\n        except BridgeError as exc:\n            return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Evidence removed.\",\n                              mk=\"ok\", extra=f\"undo_ev={hyp_id}:{side}:{quote(label)}\")\n\n    ref = {\"kind\": kind or \"observation\", \"id\": ref_id or label, \"label\": label}\n    try:\n        jobs_bridge.add_evidence(job_id, hyp_id, side, ref, by=by.strip() or None)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\",\n                          msg=f\"Evidence {'for' if side == 'for' else 'against'} added.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/delete\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def hypothesis_delete(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n                            by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                            step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Fix #2: Delete, soft (``jobs_bridge.delete_hypothesis``) -- the card\n    itself stays on the audit trail; the undo offered in the toast is\n    :func:`hypothesis_undelete` below.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        jobs_bridge.delete_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, by=by.strip() or None)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=\"hypotheses\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=\"hypotheses\", msg=\"Hypothesis deleted.\", mk=\"ok\",\n                          extra=f\"undo_hyp={hyp_id}\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/undelete\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def hypothesis_undelete(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str, hyp_id: str,\n                              by: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                              step: str = Form(default=\"7\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    try:\n        jobs_bridge.undelete_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, by=by.strip() or None)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=str(exc), mk=\"err\")\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=f\"hyp-{hyp_id}\", msg=\"Hypothesis restored.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/actions\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def action_add(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str,\n                     kind: str = Form(...), text: str = Form(...),\n                     step: str = Form(default=\"9\")) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Step 9: record one repair action -- test, inspection, repair, part,\n    clear, or a free-text note.\"\"\"\n    jobs_bridge.add_action(job_id, kind, text)\n    return _step_redirect(vin, step, anchor=\"actions\", msg=\"Action recorded.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/tools-review\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def tools_review_add(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"Step 12: the mandatory \"tools used\" review -- what was actually used\n    at release, right/wrong/unsure with a reason, anything missing, and\n    what he'd buy next time. Field names are dynamic (one triplet per\n    recommended tool, keyed by tool key) because the recommended-tool list\n    itself is dynamic, so this reads the raw form rather than a fixed\n    Pydantic/Form model -- same reasoning job_page's tools panel is built\n    for a variable-length list.\n    \"\"\"\n    form = await request.form()\n\n    def _get(key: str) -> str:\n        v = form.get(key)\n        return str(v).strip() if v is not None else \"\"\n\n    step = _get(\"step\") or \"diagnostics\"\n    tools_used: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for key in form.keys():\n        if key.startswith(\"used__\") and _get(key):\n            tool_key = key[len(\"used__\"):]\n            tools_used.append({\n                \"tool\": tool_key,\n                \"was_right\": _get(f\"right__{tool_key}\") or \"unsure\",\n                \"note\": _get(f\"note__{tool_key}\"),\n            })\n    for i in range(1, 4):\n        name = _get(f\"extra{i}_name\")\n        if name:\n            tools_used.append({\n                \"tool\": name,\n                \"was_right\": _get(f\"extra{i}_right\") or \"unsure\",\n                \"note\": _get(f\"extra{i}_note\"),\n            })\n\n    missing_tools = [m.strip() for m in _get(\"missing_tools\").split(\",\") if m.strip()]\n\n    would_buy: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for i in range(1, 4):\n        name = _get(f\"buy{i}_name\")\n        if name:\n            would_buy.append({\"name\": name, \"why\": _get(f\"buy{i}_why\")})\n\n    time_min_raw = _get(\"time_min\")\n    time_min = float(time_min_raw) if time_min_raw else None\n\n    jobs_bridge.add_tool_usage(vin, step, job_id, by=_get(\"by\"), tools_used=tools_used,\n                               missing_tools=missing_tools, would_buy=would_buy,\n                               time_min=time_min)\n    return _step_redirect(vin, \"12\", anchor=\"outcome\", msg=\"Tools review saved.\", mk=\"ok\")\n\n\n@router.post(\"/v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/close\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def job_close(request: Request, vin: str, job_id: str,\n                    outcome: str = Form(...),\n                    codes_returned: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                    verdict: str = Form(default=\"\"),\n                    tools_review_skip_reason: str = Form(default=\"\")) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"Step 12: close the case. Outcome is required -- a job can never be\n    closed with no stated result. Also gated on the tools-used review\n    (see ``jobs_bridge.close_job``) -- ``tools_review_skip_reason`` lets a\n    mechanic close without filling the review, but only by stating why.\"\"\"\n    codes = [c.strip() for c in codes_returned.split(\",\") if c.strip()]\n    error = None\n    try:\n        jobs_bridge.close_job(job_id, outcome, codes_returned=codes or None,\n                              verdict=verdict or None,\n                              tools_review_skip_reason=tools_review_skip_reason)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        error = str(exc)\n    # Rendered directly (no redirect) -- the close form lives on step 12's\n    # screen, so that's the screen the re-render must show, regardless of\n    # the flow's own current-step opinion, or a refusal would render onto\n    # whatever step happens to be current and never be seen.\n    return _job_page(request, vin, job_id=job_id, close_error=error, step=\"12\")\n\n\n__all__ = [\"router\"]\n","numLines":466,"startLine":1,"totalLines":466}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5d8b931e-763a-488e-a997-cbea54c4b039","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"d0b4838c-932a-4383-b0b8-cb25b03a5624","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad57b07152710b373","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14933406 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"af0d3d8b-5e99-49f7-ab8b-8f4f145eefc7","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:54:59.769Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14933406 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"af0d3d8b-5e99-49f7-ab8b-8f4f145eefc7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad57b07152710b373","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqMft8EL4ZwnWb8vXvbu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10754,"cache_read_input_tokens":66414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10754,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1b634c19-5dfe-42c7-916a-a4e71ed8a7f1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfqMfss7DUUqJuj3QW9zF","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b13718fd-8276-431d-98e6-54390d011c3f","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:55:04.908Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"b13718fd-8276-431d-98e6-54390d011c3f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad57b07152710b373","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqMft8EL4ZwnWb8vXvbu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gb6FCpaBVSEMtxEingAzv7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10754,"cache_read_input_tokens":66414,"output_tokens":320,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":232},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10754},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":320,"cache_read_input_tokens":66414,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10754,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10754,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Gb6FCpaBVSEMtxEingAzv7":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1b634c19-5dfe-42c7-916a-a4e71ed8a7f1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfqMfss7DUUqJuj3QW9zF","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a0e42f71-4d10-4d2d-962e-dc7d79c80899","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:55:05.690Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"a0e42f71-4d10-4d2d-962e-dc7d79c80899","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b6cba788-ea7d-4fd0-94b4-156483cb0164","agentId":"ad57b07152710b373","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gb6FCpaBVSEMtxEingAzv7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CUORE — UX/UI fixes from E2E diagnosis test\n2\t\n3\t**Tested:** `/v/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/job`, Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T, EVAP codes P0440/P0455/P0456, at a tablet-portrait width (~710 px), on 2026-10-08.\n4\t**Flow tested:** Step 5 Understand the fault → Step 6 Tests → Step 7 add a hypothesis by hand → set its status → Step 8.\n5\t**Overall:** The diagnostic content is very strong: sourced confidence, fault trees, the fuel-level gate on the EVAP monitor and tool alternatives. The problem is the workflow shell around it. It lets a tech confirm a root cause with zero evidence, and it moves them to the next step without telling them. For a tool that promises \"high correctness,\" that's the main thing to fix.\n6\t\n7\tFixes are ordered by priority. Each one has a **Fix** and an **Accept when** line that Claude Code can implement and test against.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## P0 — Diagnostic correctness (these block the main promise)\n12\t\n13\t### 1. You can confirm a hypothesis with zero evidence\n14\t**Seen:** I added \"Cracked EVAP purge line…\", tapped `confirmed` once, and it was saved. The card still showed *Evidence for: none yet*, all EVAP tests were 0/6, and the Bench page itself said \"Cannot verify yet: fuel 93.73 %, EVAP monitor will not run.\" There was no warning and no confirm dialog.\n15\t**Fix (guided-diagnostics pattern):**\n16\t- Status should follow a set path: `open → supported → confirmed`, plus `refuted` from any state. You can't jump from `open` straight to `confirmed`.\n17\t- `confirmed` requires at least 1 linked *evidence-for* item that is a test result (not only a code or freeze frame) and 0 unresolved *evidence-against* items.\n18\t- If the rule isn't met, disable the button and show the reason inline, for example: \"Needs a passed/failed test result linked. Next: Smoke test EVAP system.\"\n19\t- If the vehicle has an active blocker (such as the fuel window or a monitor that can't run), show it on the card as a warning chip.\n20\t- Confirming opens a modal that summarizes the evidence and asks the tech to tap again. Record who confirmed it and when.\n21\t**Accept when:** POSTing `confirmed` on a hypothesis with no linked test result returns 409 with a message, and the UI shows that message. The step 7 summary never says \"a hypothesis confirmed\" for an unproven hypothesis.\n22\t\n23\t### 2. There's no way to attach evidence to a hypothesis\n24\t**Seen:** The manual hypothesis card only offers four status buttons. You can't add evidence, link a test, edit, or delete it. I couldn't remove my test hypothesis, so it's still on the case with status `open`.\n25\t**Fix:**\n26\t- Each card gets **+ Evidence for** / **+ Evidence against** controls. These open a picker of on-file items: DTCs, freeze frames, live readings, completed test rows from step 6, and a free-text observation.\n27\t- Add **Edit** and **Delete** (soft-delete with Undo), and an audit trail.\n28\t**Accept when:** A tech can link a step 6 test result to a hypothesis in 2 taps or fewer, and the link shows on both the test row and the hypothesis card.\n29\t\n30\t### 3. Test rows only record \"done\", not a result\n31\t**Seen:** Step 6 rows are a single checkbox (\"Mark not done\"/done + timestamp). A smoke test that *found* a leak and one that found nothing are saved the same way.\n32\t**Fix (scan-tool test pattern):** Ticking a row opens a result sheet with:\n33\t- **Result:** Pass / Fail / Inconclusive / Not possible (with a reason)\n34\t- **Measured value + unit** when the test has a spec (with known-good band shown), plus an optional photo\n35\t- **Which hypothesis does this support or refute?** (pre-selected by system)\n36\tOnly Fail/Pass results count as evidence for #1.\n37\t**Accept when:** Every completed test row stores `result`, and optionally `value`, `unit` and `hypothesis_id`, and shows a coloured result chip.\n38\t\n39\t### 4. Step status marks steps \"green\" when nothing has been done\n40\t**Seen:** Step 6 was shown green (\"inspection, actuator run, or live observation on file\") while all checklists were 0/6, 0/3, 0/3, 0/2, 0/2 and 0/6. Step 5 turned green after a hypothesis was added on step 7.\n41\t**Fix:** Use three explicit states for every step: **Not started / In progress (n of m) / Complete**. Each state comes from real criteria, and the counts are shown in the stepper (\"6 · Tests 0/22\").\n42\t**Accept when:** With 0 tests done, step 6 shows \"Not started 0/22\" in a neutral (not green) colour.\n43\t\n44\t### 5. The app moves to the next step on its own\n45\t**Seen:** Setting the status to `confirmed` jumped the whole job to Step 8 \"Plan the repair\". Ticking a test checkbox on Step 6 **navigated away from JOB to the BENCH tab** (`/v/…#open-work`).\n46\t**Fix:** An action should never change the screen or tab. After saving, stay in place, keep the scroll position, and show a toast with **Undo**. Only move forward when the tech taps the primary **Next** button.\n47\t**Accept when:** All form posts on `/job` redirect back to `/job?step=<same>#<anchor-of-the-row>`, and a toast confirms the save.\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## P1 — Navigation and orientation\n52\t\n53\t### 6. The sticky header shows the wrong step\n54\t**Seen:** At `?step=7`, the header read \"Step 5 of 12: Understand the fault\". At `?step=6`, it read \"Step 8 of 12: Plan the repair\". The header follows the job's server-side \"current step\", not the step being viewed.\n55\t**Fix:** The header shows the step being viewed. If that's different from the job's progress, add a secondary chip: \"Job is at step 8 →\".\n56\t\n57\t### 7. The primary button links to the current page\n58\t**Seen:** On step 5, the red **Review the code** button's href is `?step=5`, so tapping it does nothing.\n59\t**Fix:** The primary button is always **Next: <next step name> →**, or a specific action that moves the job forward. The secondary button is **← Back**. Use the same placement on every step: bottom-right on tablet, sticky bottom bar on mobile, as scan tools do.\n60\t\n61\t### 8. The stepper isn't usable\n62\t**Seen:** The row `1 2 3 … 12` is bare numbers in about 11 px green text. Below it is a full list of all 12 steps, so every screen opens with a large amount of chrome before any content. The intro paragraph (\"…nothing here is a second copy of the truth\") is developer copy.\n63\t**Fix:**\n64\t- Replace both with one compact stepper: number + short label + state icon (done ✓ / in-progress ◐ / blocked ⚠ / todo ○). Group them into phases: **Intake (1–4) · Diagnose (5–7) · Repair (8–9) · Close-out (10–12)**.\n65\t- Collapse the step list into the `Steps ▾` menu.\n66\t- Remove the intro paragraph.\n67\t**Accept when:** The current step's content starts within the first 200 px below the sticky header.\n68\t\n69\t### 9. The vehicle banner is unclear and inconsistent\n70\t**Seen:** The Job page says \"(unnamed vehicle)\" / \"…B88115\", while Bench says \"Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0 Turbo 16V MultiAir\". Raw enums such as `MES not_running` and `UNVERIFIED_REPAIR` show in the UI. The \"Next: Understand the fault →\" chip wraps across 4 lines.\n71\t**Fix:**\n72\t- One persistent vehicle banner, the same on every tab: **Year Make Model Engine · VIN last 8 · odometer · connection state** (`Scanner: disconnected`, using human labels).\n73\t- Map every enum to a display label.\n74\t- The \"Next\" chip becomes a single-line pill or is removed (it duplicates #7).\n75\t\n76\t### 10. Step numbers referenced in content don't match\n77\t**Seen:** Step 8 says \"Record your decision… in the step 7 'Would buy next time' review\", but step 7 is Hypotheses.\n78\t**Fix:** Generate cross-references from the step registry (`step_link('review')`). Don't hard-code numbers.\n79\t\n80\t---\n81\t\n82\t## P1 — The hypothesis screen (step 7) layout\n83\t\n84\t### 11. Suggestions crowd out the tech's own hypotheses, and there are duplicates\n85\t**Seen:** 16 suggested cards with dashed borders, most saying \"Evidence for: none yet\". Eight of them are copies of \"Upstream check\" with the same text. The tech's own form is at the very bottom, and the \"Add a hypothesis\" heading appears twice.\n86\t**Fix:**\n87\t- **Order:** Active hypotheses (ranked) → *Add hypothesis* (collapsed button at top) → Suggestions.\n88\t- Rank suggestions by the amount of evidence that supports them. Show only the top 3 and put the rest under \"Show 13 more\".\n89\t- Merge suggestions that share the same test into one card that lists the affected codes (\"Upstream check: Network/CAN — B1029, B102E, B1040, B1176\").\n90\t- Visually separate suggestions that have no evidence at all.\n91\t- Before adding a hypothesis, check whether a similar one already exists, for example \"Similar to *EVAP: ESIM signal path* — merge?\"\n92\t\n93\t### 12. The manual hypothesis form is too small and not guided enough\n94\t**Seen:** There are 3 free-text inputs about 170 px wide; the Hypothesis input cuts off its own text. Validation is only the browser's native tooltip. System is free text, so values like \"EVAP\"/\"evap\"/\"Evap system\" will split the data.\n95\t**Fix:**\n96\t- Make the inputs full width.\n97\t- **System** is a select populated from the systems taxonomy the code cards already use.\n98\t- Add **Linked codes** (multi-select of open DTCs, pre-filled from system) and **Initial likelihood** (Low/Med/High).\n99\t- **Next test** offers suggestions from the fault tree.\n100\t- Show inline validation messages.\n101\t\n102\t### 13. Hypothesis cards are missing key information\n103\t**Fix:** Each card shows a likelihood bar, counts of evidence for and against, the linked codes, the next test with a **Do it now →** deep-link to that row on step 6, and the last-updated time. Pin the leading hypothesis at the top.\n104\t\n105\t---\n106\t\n107\t## P2 — Readability and touch (shop-floor conditions)\n108\t\n109\t### 14. Text is too small and too low-contrast for a shop floor\n110\t**Measured on step 7:**\n111\t- Body text is 13 px. Muted text in `#79848C` appears 111 times at 10–13 px, and some green labels are 10 px.\n112\t- Evidence chips are all-caps monospace green-on-dark (`P0455-00 FREEZE FRAME: ABOVE 85 %…`), which is hard to read quickly.\n113\t\n114\t**Fix:**\n115\t- Body text at least 16 px, secondary text at least 14 px, nothing below 12 px.\n116\t- Muted text at least 4.5:1 contrast against the background (`#79848C` → about `#9AA4AC` or lighter).\n117\t- Evidence chips in sentence case with a code-ID prefix in monospace only.\n118\t\n119\t### 15. Touch targets are too small\n120\t**Measured:** 28 of 83 interactive elements are smaller than 44 px. The top tabs are 40 px tall, the `MORE…` tab is 33 px, the `±` row buttons are about 17 px, and some full-width toggles are 21 px tall. A tech wearing gloves will miss them.\n121\t**Fix:** Make every interactive element at least 48×48 px, matching scan-tool tablets. The `±` \"flag row\" control needs a clear label or icon plus a tooltip, because right now it looks like an expand control.\n122\t\n123\t### 16. Code cards use the wrong visual weight\n124\t**Seen:** The DTC is shown twice (a small `P0456` and then a huge 40 px `P0456`). System tags are underlined like links. The drivability symptom chips (`ROUGH_IDLE`, `HESITATION`…) use strikethrough to mean \"not expected\", which looks like a \"deleted\" or error state.\n125\t**Fix:**\n126\t- Show the DTC once in the header row with its status (Current/Pending/History), MIL state and confidence badge.\n127\t- Make system tags chips, not links.\n128\t- Symptom chips show \"Expected ✓ / Not expected —\" with a legend.\n129\t- Show raw source URLs as a \"Sources (3)\" disclosure.\n130\t\n131\t### 17. The same message appears three times\n132\t**Seen:** The Bench page repeats the same \"Cannot verify yet: fuel 93.73 %…\" message 3 times (banner, card, heading).\n133\t**Fix:** Show it once as a **Blocker** banner, with an icon, a one-line action (\"Burn fuel to 15–85 %, then run drive cycle\"), and a \"Why?\" disclosure. Show the same blocker inside the Job flow on steps 7 and 10, because that's where it affects the decision.\n134\t\n135\t---\n136\t\n137\t## Suggested implementation order for Claude Code\n138\t1. #5 (no auto-navigation) + #6/#7 (header and Next button). These are small changes with a large effect.\n139\t2. #3 (test results) → #2 (evidence linking) → #1 (confirmation rules) → #4 (honest step status). #1 depends on #2 and #3.\n140\t3. #11–#13 step 7 layout.\n141\t4. #8–#10, then #14–#17 visual pass.\n142\t\n143\t**Regression test to add (E2E):** Create a hypothesis → try to confirm it (expect blocked) → record a Fail smoke test linked to it → status moves to `supported` → confirm (with modal) → the page stays on step 7 → Next goes to step 8. Run it at 768×1024 and 1280×800.\n144\t\n145\t*Test data note:* this run left one manual hypothesis on the VIN (\"Cracked EVAP purge line at canister…\", status reset to `open`). It can't be deleted from the UI (see #2). The step 6 checkbox I ticked was unticked again.\n146\t"}]},"uuid":"14d95c7e-89fc-4c50-b900-ced5dbb12389","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:55:05.720Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md","content":"# CUORE — UX/UI fixes from E2E diagnosis test\n\n**Tested:** `/v/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/job`, Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T, EVAP codes P0440/P0455/P0456, at a tablet-portrait width (~710 px), on 2026-10-08.\n**Flow tested:** Step 5 Understand the fault → Step 6 Tests → Step 7 add a hypothesis by hand → set its status → Step 8.\n**Overall:** The diagnostic content is very strong: sourced confidence, fault trees, the fuel-level gate on the EVAP monitor and tool alternatives. The problem is the workflow shell around it. It lets a tech confirm a root cause with zero evidence, and it moves them to the next step without telling them. For a tool that promises \"high correctness,\" that's the main thing to fix.\n\nFixes are ordered by priority. Each one has a **Fix** and an **Accept when** line that Claude Code can implement and test against.\n\n---\n\n## P0 — Diagnostic correctness (these block the main promise)\n\n### 1. You can confirm a hypothesis with zero evidence\n**Seen:** I added \"Cracked EVAP purge line…\", tapped `confirmed` once, and it was saved. The card still showed *Evidence for: none yet*, all EVAP tests were 0/6, and the Bench page itself said \"Cannot verify yet: fuel 93.73 %, EVAP monitor will not run.\" There was no warning and no confirm dialog.\n**Fix (guided-diagnostics pattern):**\n- Status should follow a set path: `open → supported → confirmed`, plus `refuted` from any state. You can't jump from `open` straight to `confirmed`.\n- `confirmed` requires at least 1 linked *evidence-for* item that is a test result (not only a code or freeze frame) and 0 unresolved *evidence-against* items.\n- If the rule isn't met, disable the button and show the reason inline, for example: \"Needs a passed/failed test result linked. Next: Smoke test EVAP system.\"\n- If the vehicle has an active blocker (such as the fuel window or a monitor that can't run), show it on the card as a warning chip.\n- Confirming opens a modal that summarizes the evidence and asks the tech to tap again. Record who confirmed it and when.\n**Accept when:** POSTing `confirmed` on a hypothesis with no linked test result returns 409 with a message, and the UI shows that message. The step 7 summary never says \"a hypothesis confirmed\" for an unproven hypothesis.\n\n### 2. There's no way to attach evidence to a hypothesis\n**Seen:** The manual hypothesis card only offers four status buttons. You can't add evidence, link a test, edit, or delete it. I couldn't remove my test hypothesis, so it's still on the case with status `open`.\n**Fix:**\n- Each card gets **+ Evidence for** / **+ Evidence against** controls. These open a picker of on-file items: DTCs, freeze frames, live readings, completed test rows from step 6, and a free-text observation.\n- Add **Edit** and **Delete** (soft-delete with Undo), and an audit trail.\n**Accept when:** A tech can link a step 6 test result to a hypothesis in 2 taps or fewer, and the link shows on both the test row and the hypothesis card.\n\n### 3. Test rows only record \"done\", not a result\n**Seen:** Step 6 rows are a single checkbox (\"Mark not done\"/done + timestamp). A smoke test that *found* a leak and one that found nothing are saved the same way.\n**Fix (scan-tool test pattern):** Ticking a row opens a result sheet with:\n- **Result:** Pass / Fail / Inconclusive / Not possible (with a reason)\n- **Measured value + unit** when the test has a spec (with known-good band shown), plus an optional photo\n- **Which hypothesis does this support or refute?** (pre-selected by system)\nOnly Fail/Pass results count as evidence for #1.\n**Accept when:** Every completed test row stores `result`, and optionally `value`, `unit` and `hypothesis_id`, and shows a coloured result chip.\n\n### 4. Step status marks steps \"green\" when nothing has been done\n**Seen:** Step 6 was shown green (\"inspection, actuator run, or live observation on file\") while all checklists were 0/6, 0/3, 0/3, 0/2, 0/2 and 0/6. Step 5 turned green after a hypothesis was added on step 7.\n**Fix:** Use three explicit states for every step: **Not started / In progress (n of m) / Complete**. Each state comes from real criteria, and the counts are shown in the stepper (\"6 · Tests 0/22\").\n**Accept when:** With 0 tests done, step 6 shows \"Not started 0/22\" in a neutral (not green) colour.\n\n### 5. The app moves to the next step on its own\n**Seen:** Setting the status to `confirmed` jumped the whole job to Step 8 \"Plan the repair\". Ticking a test checkbox on Step 6 **navigated away from JOB to the BENCH tab** (`/v/…#open-work`).\n**Fix:** An action should never change the screen or tab. After saving, stay in place, keep the scroll position, and show a toast with **Undo**. Only move forward when the tech taps the primary **Next** button.\n**Accept when:** All form posts on `/job` redirect back to `/job?step=<same>#<anchor-of-the-row>`, and a toast confirms the save.\n\n---\n\n## P1 — Navigation and orientation\n\n### 6. The sticky header shows the wrong step\n**Seen:** At `?step=7`, the header read \"Step 5 of 12: Understand the fault\". At `?step=6`, it read \"Step 8 of 12: Plan the repair\". The header follows the job's server-side \"current step\", not the step being viewed.\n**Fix:** The header shows the step being viewed. If that's different from the job's progress, add a secondary chip: \"Job is at step 8 →\".\n\n### 7. The primary button links to the current page\n**Seen:** On step 5, the red **Review the code** button's href is `?step=5`, so tapping it does nothing.\n**Fix:** The primary button is always **Next: <next step name> →**, or a specific action that moves the job forward. The secondary button is **← Back**. Use the same placement on every step: bottom-right on tablet, sticky bottom bar on mobile, as scan tools do.\n\n### 8. The stepper isn't usable\n**Seen:** The row `1 2 3 … 12` is bare numbers in about 11 px green text. Below it is a full list of all 12 steps, so every screen opens with a large amount of chrome before any content. The intro paragraph (\"…nothing here is a second copy of the truth\") is developer copy.\n**Fix:**\n- Replace both with one compact stepper: number + short label + state icon (done ✓ / in-progress ◐ / blocked ⚠ / todo ○). Group them into phases: **Intake (1–4) · Diagnose (5–7) · Repair (8–9) · Close-out (10–12)**.\n- Collapse the step list into the `Steps ▾` menu.\n- Remove the intro paragraph.\n**Accept when:** The current step's content starts within the first 200 px below the sticky header.\n\n### 9. The vehicle banner is unclear and inconsistent\n**Seen:** The Job page says \"(unnamed vehicle)\" / \"…B88115\", while Bench says \"Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0 Turbo 16V MultiAir\". Raw enums such as `MES not_running` and `UNVERIFIED_REPAIR` show in the UI. The \"Next: Understand the fault →\" chip wraps across 4 lines.\n**Fix:**\n- One persistent vehicle banner, the same on every tab: **Year Make Model Engine · VIN last 8 · odometer · connection state** (`Scanner: disconnected`, using human labels).\n- Map every enum to a display label.\n- The \"Next\" chip becomes a single-line pill or is removed (it duplicates #7).\n\n### 10. Step numbers referenced in content don't match\n**Seen:** Step 8 says \"Record your decision… in the step 7 'Would buy next time' review\", but step 7 is Hypotheses.\n**Fix:** Generate cross-references from the step registry (`step_link('review')`). Don't hard-code numbers.\n\n---\n\n## P1 — The hypothesis screen (step 7) layout\n\n### 11. Suggestions crowd out the tech's own hypotheses, and there are duplicates\n**Seen:** 16 suggested cards with dashed borders, most saying \"Evidence for: none yet\". Eight of them are copies of \"Upstream check\" with the same text. The tech's own form is at the very bottom, and the \"Add a hypothesis\" heading appears twice.\n**Fix:**\n- **Order:** Active hypotheses (ranked) → *Add hypothesis* (collapsed button at top) → Suggestions.\n- Rank suggestions by the amount of evidence that supports them. Show only the top 3 and put the rest under \"Show 13 more\".\n- Merge suggestions that share the same test into one card that lists the affected codes (\"Upstream check: Network/CAN — B1029, B102E, B1040, B1176\").\n- Visually separate suggestions that have no evidence at all.\n- Before adding a hypothesis, check whether a similar one already exists, for example \"Similar to *EVAP: ESIM signal path* — merge?\"\n\n### 12. The manual hypothesis form is too small and not guided enough\n**Seen:** There are 3 free-text inputs about 170 px wide; the Hypothesis input cuts off its own text. Validation is only the browser's native tooltip. System is free text, so values like \"EVAP\"/\"evap\"/\"Evap system\" will split the data.\n**Fix:**\n- Make the inputs full width.\n- **System** is a select populated from the systems taxonomy the code cards already use.\n- Add **Linked codes** (multi-select of open DTCs, pre-filled from system) and **Initial likelihood** (Low/Med/High).\n- **Next test** offers suggestions from the fault tree.\n- Show inline validation messages.\n\n### 13. Hypothesis cards are missing key information\n**Fix:** Each card shows a likelihood bar, counts of evidence for and against, the linked codes, the next test with a **Do it now →** deep-link to that row on step 6, and the last-updated time. Pin the leading hypothesis at the top.\n\n---\n\n## P2 — Readability and touch (shop-floor conditions)\n\n### 14. Text is too small and too low-contrast for a shop floor\n**Measured on step 7:**\n- Body text is 13 px. Muted text in `#79848C` appears 111 times at 10–13 px, and some green labels are 10 px.\n- Evidence chips are all-caps monospace green-on-dark (`P0455-00 FREEZE FRAME: ABOVE 85 %…`), which is hard to read quickly.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Body text at least 16 px, secondary text at least 14 px, nothing below 12 px.\n- Muted text at least 4.5:1 contrast against the background (`#79848C` → about `#9AA4AC` or lighter).\n- Evidence chips in sentence case with a code-ID prefix in monospace only.\n\n### 15. Touch targets are too small\n**Measured:** 28 of 83 interactive elements are smaller than 44 px. The top tabs are 40 px tall, the `MORE…` tab is 33 px, the `±` row buttons are about 17 px, and some full-width toggles are 21 px tall. A tech wearing gloves will miss them.\n**Fix:** Make every interactive element at least 48×48 px, matching scan-tool tablets. The `±` \"flag row\" control needs a clear label or icon plus a tooltip, because right now it looks like an expand control.\n\n### 16. Code cards use the wrong visual weight\n**Seen:** The DTC is shown twice (a small `P0456` and then a huge 40 px `P0456`). System tags are underlined like links. The drivability symptom chips (`ROUGH_IDLE`, `HESITATION`…) use strikethrough to mean \"not expected\", which looks like a \"deleted\" or error state.\n**Fix:**\n- Show the DTC once in the header row with its status (Current/Pending/History), MIL state and confidence badge.\n- Make system tags chips, not links.\n- Symptom chips show \"Expected ✓ / Not expected —\" with a legend.\n- Show raw source URLs as a \"Sources (3)\" disclosure.\n\n### 17. The same message appears three times\n**Seen:** The Bench page repeats the same \"Cannot verify yet: fuel 93.73 %…\" message 3 times (banner, card, heading).\n**Fix:** Show it once as a **Blocker** banner, with an icon, a one-line action (\"Burn fuel to 15–85 %, then run drive cycle\"), and a \"Why?\" disclosure. Show the same blocker inside the Job flow on steps 7 and 10, because that's where it affects the decision.\n\n---\n\n## Suggested implementation order for Claude Code\n1. #5 (no auto-navigation) + #6/#7 (header and Next button). These are small changes with a large effect.\n2. #3 (test results) → #2 (evidence linking) → #1 (confirmation rules) → #4 (honest step status). #1 depends on #2 and #3.\n3. #11–#13 step 7 layout.\n4. #8–#10, then #14–#17 visual pass.\n\n**Regression test to add (E2E):** Create a hypothesis → try to confirm it (expect blocked) → record a Fail smoke test linked to it → status moves to `supported` → confirm (with modal) → the page stays on step 7 → Next goes to step 8. Run it at 768×1024 and 1280×800.\n\n*Test data note:* this run left one manual hypothesis on the VIN (\"Cracked EVAP purge line at canister…\", status reset to `open`). It can't be deleted from the UI (see #2). The step 6 checkbox I ticked was unticked again.\n","numLines":146,"startLine":1,"totalLines":146}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a0e42f71-4d10-4d2d-962e-dc7d79c80899","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
