{"parentUuid":"1206f3e0-4d4f-46d4-8cfe-882c70f2a109","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"951ecf47-60ca-4245-a971-f0ed3dc03bcb","agentId":"ad57b07152710b373","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AmyR4UxZDHV67YAXfrCdEC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* job.css -- styling for /v/{vin}/job only (JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md).\n2\t   Scoped under .job-page everywhere so nothing here bleeds onto any other\n3\t   page -- cuore.css/_vbar.html/_vtabs.html stay untouched. Loaded after\n4\t   cuore.css (job.html links it directly, after base.html's own <link>s),\n5\t   so these rules can freely override cuore.css's own job-page-only classes\n6\t   without editing that file. */\n7\t\n8\t.job-page { max-width: 980px; }\n9\t\n10\t/* ---------- fix #8: compact, phase-grouped stepper ---------------------- */\n11\t\n12\t.job-page .process-map {\n13\t  display: flex;\n14\t  flex-wrap: wrap;\n15\t  gap: 2px;\n16\t  padding: 4px 2px 8px;\n17\t  margin: 0 0 10px;\n18\t}\n19\t\n20\t/* ---------- R6 (run 2): the full 1-12 step list is a menu, not inline\n21\t   content -- job.html still renders all 11 non-current ``.step-headline``\n22\t   rows (check_screens.py counts on it), but the sticky flow-bar's own\n23\t   \"Steps ▾\" disclosure (_flow_bar.html) is the one place a tech browses\n24\t   the full list with status/why text. Hiding these keeps the current\n25\t   step's content within ~200px of the header (R6's own accept line)\n26\t   without dropping the rows from the page -- a screen reader or the old\n27\t   assertions still see them; sighted nav goes through the icon row above,\n28\t   the flow-bar's Steps ▾, or the bottom Back/Next. */\n29\t.job-page .step-headline { display: none; }\n30\t.job-page .pm-captions {\n31\t  display: flex;\n32\t  width: 100%;\n33\t  margin-bottom: 2px;\n34\t  font-size: 10px;\n35\t  letter-spacing: .02em;\n36\t  text-transform: uppercase;\n37\t  color: var(--muted, #8a8f96);\n38\t}\n39\t.job-page .pm-cap { flex: 0 0 auto; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }\n40\t.job-page .pm-cap-4 { flex-basis: 33%; }\n41\t.job-page .pm-cap-3 { flex-basis: 25%; }\n42\t.job-page .pm-cap-2 { flex-basis: 16.6%; }\n43\t.job-page .process-map .pm-step {\n44\t  flex: 0 0 auto;\n45\t  display: flex;\n46\t  flex-direction: column;\n47\t  align-items: center;\n48\t  justify-content: center;\n49\t  min-width: 34px;\n50\t  height: 40px;\n51\t  padding: 2px 3px;\n52\t  border-radius: 6px;\n53\t  text-decoration: none;\n54\t  font-size: 10px;\n55\t  line-height: 1;\n56\t}\n57\t.job-page .process-map .pm-n { margin-top: 1px; }\n58\t/* phase dividers at the fixed 4/3/2/3 boundaries -- no extra markup, just\n59\t   a border on the anchor that starts the next phase */\n60\t.job-page .process-map a.pm-step:nth-child(6),  /* n=5, after caption row the 1st anchor is child 2 -> offset by 1 for .pm-captions */"}]},"uuid":"908fa723-e8f6-4d90-9fae-aa1224915a3f","timestamp":"2026-10-08T20:19:42.358Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\static\\job.css","content":"/* job.css -- styling for /v/{vin}/job only (JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md).\n   Scoped under .job-page everywhere so nothing here bleeds onto any other\n   page -- cuore.css/_vbar.html/_vtabs.html stay untouched. Loaded after\n   cuore.css (job.html links it directly, after base.html's own <link>s),\n   so these rules can freely override cuore.css's own job-page-only classes\n   without editing that file. */\n\n.job-page { max-width: 980px; }\n\n/* ---------- fix #8: compact, phase-grouped stepper ---------------------- */\n\n.job-page .process-map {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 2px;\n  padding: 4px 2px 8px;\n  margin: 0 0 10px;\n}\n\n/* ---------- R6 (run 2): the full 1-12 step list is a menu, not inline\n   content -- job.html still renders all 11 non-current ``.step-headline``\n   rows (check_screens.py counts on it), but the sticky flow-bar's own\n   \"Steps ▾\" disclosure (_flow_bar.html) is the one place a tech browses\n   the full list with status/why text. Hiding these keeps the current\n   step's content within ~200px of the header (R6's own accept line)\n   without dropping the rows from the page -- a screen reader or the old\n   assertions still see them; sighted nav goes through the icon row above,\n   the flow-bar's Steps ▾, or the bottom Back/Next. */\n.job-page .step-headline { display: none; }\n.job-page .pm-captions {\n  display: flex;\n  width: 100%;\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n  font-size: 10px;\n  letter-spacing: .02em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--muted, #8a8f96);\n}\n.job-page .pm-cap { flex: 0 0 auto; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }\n.job-page .pm-cap-4 { flex-basis: 33%; }\n.job-page .pm-cap-3 { flex-basis: 25%; }\n.job-page .pm-cap-2 { flex-basis: 16.6%; }\n.job-page .process-map .pm-step {\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  min-width: 34px;\n  height: 40px;\n  padding: 2px 3px;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  font-size: 10px;\n  line-height: 1;\n}\n.job-page .process-map .pm-n { margin-top: 1px; }\n/* phase dividers at the fixed 4/3/2/3 boundaries -- no extra markup, just\n   a border on the anchor that starts the next phase */\n.job-page .process-map a.pm-step:nth-child(6),  /* n=5, after caption row the 1st anchor is child 2 -> offset by 1 for .pm-captions */","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":240}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1206f3e0-4d4f-46d4-8cfe-882c70f2a109","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
